          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The joint library hosted a fascinating lunchtime talk on Sacred Trash in Medieval Damascus on Wednesday 11 November.  The talk saw Dr Hirschler address some of the current challenges  in accessing manuscripts at the present time in Syria and share fascinating insights into the research that has informed his upcoming book, Medieval Damascus: Plurality and Diversity in an Arabic Library - The Ashrafīya Library Catalogue which will be published next year.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
